hint: Loop over `d.items()` and unpack each pair as `k, v`.
hint: Write the old value first, as the new key: `v: k`.
hint: `return {v: k for k, v in d.items()}`
right: Unpacking each pair as `k, v` and writing `v: k` at the front swaps them. When values repeat, the later pair replaces the earlier one, the same as any repeated key.
